---
description: boxed_piston FDTD study conventions
globs: proj/boxed_piston/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Only read/write code. Never run code, tests, or git commands.
- Reply and write code/comments/docs in US English.
- Spec: proj/boxed_piston/docs/brief.md. The brief describes the current
  state only, with no history.
- Do not change kernel, CPML, or source semantics unless explicitly asked.
- Time convention e^{+jωt}; numpy forward FFT as-is, no conjugation.
- Time levels: after step(n), p is at (n+1)Δt and v at (n+½)Δt. Post code
  reads time arrays from the HDF5 file and never reconstructs them from n.
- Scalar hygiene: use .item() or np.squeeze; no float() on arrays; helpers
  return scalars for scalar input and preserve the input dtype.
- Tests: pytest, fast by default; mark anything over ~5 s with the slow marker.
- Validation scripts follow c01–c03: progress printouts, require_ram,
  results JSON via to_json_safe.
- End each reply with: files changed, assumed signatures, open issues.